what i want to talk about is as you may  have noticed we live in a culture that  seems to have  completely lost its mind  we are  living through a period of mass  psychosis that is very truly  unprecedented in the history of human  civilization it seems as though all at  once millions of our countrymen  sort of woke up one day having forgot  some of the most basic facts about  reality like a giant epidemic of just  the weirdest sort of amnesia  and lying at the heart of this  intellectual chaos is the confusion or  apparent confusion anyway  over human biology  a a mental disease called gender  ideology has gripped hold of a large  swath of the american public  and totally taken over almost all of our  or in fact all of our most powerful  institutions  the disciples of this cult have been  convinced or pretend to be convinced  anyway that men are women women are men  that you know men can have babies women  can have penises that a woman can  impregnate a man who can then give birth  to and breastfeed a child  that's somehow the most basic facts  about reality and about biology facts  which all people everywhere across the  entire world for thousands and thousands  of years all recognized intuitively  are no longer valid  it's total madness and it's a madness  which has infected our society and now  is threatening i think to tear it apart  at the seams already is in fact doing  that  it was for this reason that i along with  my uh extraordinary team at the daily  wire decided that we had to make a film  which just premiered on the daily wire  and has angered the left so much that  there was even  and still is a sustained cyber attack on  the site to shut us down and prevent  people from seeing it  along with all the other tricks they're  they're pulling around this thing  the film is called what is a woman and  it documents  my year-long journey to confront and  expose gender ideology  uh it was a journey that took us all  over the the country from san francisco  to seattle to new york  many places in between  it took us even across the world deep  into the bush in kenya  took us to other third world countries  too like los angeles for example  now  our goal broadly was to  explore gender ideology to kind of show  it for what it is  and as the title suggests this larger  goal centers around one seemingly quite  simple and specific question  what is a woman
 

